+## Sprite sheets
+
+A sheet only pays off when everything on it shows at the same time. So the controller and touch
+prompts are split by device: a player only ever sees one device's set, and loading the other two
+would waste memory.
+
+Each piece's `ImageRectOffset` skips the cell margin and its `ImageRectSize` covers only the art. That
+way the art fills the `ImageLabel` exactly.
+
+Common `ImageLabel` setup for a sheet piece:
+
+| Property | Value |
+|---|---|
+| `Image` | the sheet's asset id |
+| `ImageRectOffset` | from the piece's row in the tables below |
+| `ImageRectSize` | the sheet's art size |
+| `Size` | `UDim2.fromOffset(w, h)` at the 1080p size |
+| `ScaleType` | `Fit` |
+| `BackgroundTransparency` | `1` |
+| `ImageColor3` | the tint for white sheets, `(255,255,255)` for full-color sheets |
+
+Check every sheet on a real phone before shipping. People have reported sprite rects landing on the
+wrong piece on some phones and consoles while desktop drew them correctly.
+
