+## Native visuals (nothing to export)
+
+### N1 KeyPrompt: keyboard keys (`40:13`–`40:31`)
+
+All ten keys are a rounded box with a solid inside stroke and a text label. Roblox draws all of that
+natively, and a text label means rebound keys and new keys need no new art. Build one component that
+takes the key text.
+
+| Part | Properties |
+|---|---|
+| Frame | `Size` height 40. Width 40 for one character, 56 for Esc / Tab / Shift (or `AutomaticSize = X` with a 40 minimum and 8 px side padding). `BackgroundColor3 (235,237,242)` |
+| UICorner | `CornerRadius = UDim.new(0, 6)` |
+| UIStroke | `Color (153,157,171)`, `Thickness 2`, `BorderStrokePosition = Inner` |
+| TextLabel | Builder Sans **Bold**, size 18, line height 24, `TextColor3 (31,33,41)`, centered |
+
+### N2 Profile Card (`40:153`)
+
+- Frame 360 × 190, `BackgroundColor3 (33,37,54)`, `UICorner` 16.
+- **Avatar** (`40:151`): the Figma image is a placeholder photo. Per the note, use the player's
+  headshot: an ImageLabel 150 × 150 at (20, 20),
+  `Image = "rbxthumb://type=AvatarHeadShot&id=<UserId>&w=352&h=352"` (352 is the smallest valid
+  size that covers 150 × 2), `UICorner CornerRadius = UDim.new(0.5, 0)` to make it a circle,
+  `ScaleType = Crop`. **Do not export the placeholder.**
+
+### N3 Glass Card (`40:155`): approximation
+
+- Design: white at 10% fill, 1 px inside stroke of white at 20%, radius 16, **20 px background blur**.
+- Roblox can't blur what's behind a frame (`BlurEffect` blurs the whole 3D view). Use a darker,
+  more opaque fill instead: Frame 320 × 200, `BackgroundColor3 (42,44,52)` (the design's 10% white over the
+  page color), `BackgroundTransparency ≈ 0.15`, `UICorner` 16, `UIStroke` white `Transparency 0.8`
+  `Thickness 1` `BorderStrokePosition = Inner`.
+- Title: TextLabel "Inventory", Builder Sans **Bold** 22, line height 28, white, left-aligned, at (24, 20).
+
+### N4 Progress Bar (`40:158`)
+
+Note: *"Fill width follows quest progress."* The fill changes with game state, so it has to be native.
+
+- Track: Frame 300 × 12, `BackgroundColor3 (255,255,255)`, `BackgroundTransparency 0.88`, `UICorner` 6.
+- Fill: child Frame, `Size = UDim2.new(progress, 0, 1, 0)` (the design shows 0.62),
+  `BackgroundColor3 (87,209,118)`, `UICorner` 6. Below 12 px wide the rounded ends squash, so hide the fill at 0.
